1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,532
Hello, I'm delighted to welcome you to our Wildlife Club,

2
00:00:03,532 --> 00:00:07,485
and very pleased that you're interested in the countryside and the plants

3
00:00:07,485 --> 00:00:08,890
and creatures of this area.

4
00:00:08,890 --> 00:00:13,815
I think you'll be surprised at the variety we have here, even though we're

5
00:00:13,815 --> 00:00:14,900
not far from London.

6
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:20,090
I'll start by telling you about some of the parks and open spaces nearby.

7
00:00:20,090 --> 00:00:24,050
One very pleasant place is Halland Common.

8
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:27,601
This has been public land for hundreds of years,

9
00:00:27,601 --> 00:00:31,473
and what you'll find interesting is that the River Ouse,

10
00:00:31,473 --> 00:00:36,770
which flows into the sea eighty kilometres away, has its source in the common.

11
00:00:36,770 --> 00:00:41,089
There's an information board about the plants and animals you can see here,

12
00:00:41,089 --> 00:00:45,890
and by the way, the common is accessible 24 hours a day.

13
00:00:45,890 --> 00:00:48,991
Then there's Holt Island,

14
00:00:48,991 --> 00:00:51,670
which is noted for its great range of trees.

15
00:00:51,670 --> 00:00:56,792
In the past willows were grown here commercially for basket-making,

16
00:00:56,792 --> 00:01:00,850
and this ancient craft has recently been reintroduced.

17
00:01:00,850 --> 00:01:05,483
The island is only open to the public from Friday to Sunday,

18
00:01:05,483 --> 00:01:06,987
because it's quite small,

19
00:01:06,987 --> 00:01:11,039
and if there were people around every day, much of the wildlife would keep

20
00:01:11,039 --> 00:01:11,560
away.

21
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:17,410
From there it's just a short walk across the bridge to Longfield Country Park.

22
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:23,000
Longfield has a modern replica of a farm from over two thousand years ago.

23
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:29,340
Children's activities are often arranged there, like bread-making and face-painting.

24
00:01:29,340 --> 00:01:32,963
The park is only open during daylight hours,

25
00:01:32,963 --> 00:01:35,680
so bear that in mind if you decide to go there.

26
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:40,215
Longfield Park has a programme of activities throughout the year,

27
00:01:40,215 --> 00:01:44,008
and to give you a sample, this is what's happening in the next few

28
00:01:44,008 --> 00:01:44,690
days.

29
00:01:44,690 --> 00:01:48,133
On Monday you can learn about herbs,

30
00:01:48,133 --> 00:01:50,710
and how they've been used over the centuries.

31
00:01:50,710 --> 00:01:56,072
You'll start with a tour of our herb garden, practise the technique of using

32
00:01:56,072 --> 00:01:58,160
them as colour dyes for cloth.

33
00:01:58,160 --> 00:02:03,360
And listen to an illustrated talk about their use in cooking and medicine.

34
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:09,850
Then on Wednesday you can join local experts to discover the variety of insects

35
00:02:09,850 --> 00:02:12,080
and brids that appear in the evening.

36
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:16,254
We keep to a small number of people in the group,

37
00:02:16,254 --> 00:02:19,907
so if you want to go you'll need to phone the park ranger a

38
00:02:19,907 --> 00:02:20,830
few days ahead.

39
00:02:20,830 --> 00:02:22,445
There's a small charge,

40
00:02:22,445 --> 00:02:24,160
which you should pay when you turn up.

41
00:02:24,160 --> 00:02:29,743
I'm sure you're all keen to help with the practical task of looking after

42
00:02:29,743 --> 00:02:30,265
the park,

43
00:02:30,265 --> 00:02:33,880
so on Saturday you can join a working party.

44
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:39,798
You'll have a choice of all sorts of activities, from planting hedges to picking up litter

45
00:02:39,798 --> 00:02:43,689
so you'll be able to change from one to another when you feel like

46
00:02:43,689 --> 00:02:43,950
it.

47
00:02:43,950 --> 00:02:47,505
The rangers will be hard at work all day,

48
00:02:47,505 --> 00:02:51,100
but do come and join in, even for just a short while.

49
00:02:51,100 --> 00:02:56,826
One thing, though, is to make sure you're wearing something that you don't mind getting dirty

50
00:02:56,826 --> 00:02:57,730
or torn.

51
00:02:57,730 --> 00:03:04,731
And finally I'd like to tell you about our new wildlife area, Hinchingbrooke Park,

52
00:03:04,731 --> 00:03:07,580
which will be opened to the public next month.

53
00:03:07,580 --> 00:03:11,774
This slide doesn't really indicate how big it is,

54
00:03:11,774 --> 00:03:15,225
but anyway, you can see the two gates into the park,

55
00:03:15,225 --> 00:03:16,810
and the main paths.

56
00:03:16,810 --> 00:03:20,806
As you can see, there's a lake in the north west of the park,

57
00:03:20,806 --> 00:03:23,838
with a bird hide to the west of it, at the end of a

58
00:03:23,838 --> 00:03:24,420
path.

59
00:03:24,420 --> 00:03:28,750
So it'll be a nice quiet place for watching the birds on the lake.

60
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:35,579
Fairly close to where refreshments are available, there's a dog-walking area in the southern

61
00:03:35,579 --> 00:03:38,050
part of the park, leading off from the path.

62
00:03:38,050 --> 00:03:41,807
And if you just want to sit and relax, you can go to the

63
00:03:41,807 --> 00:03:42,911
flower garden;

64
00:03:42,911 --> 00:03:47,110
that's the circular area on the map surrounded by paths.

65
00:03:47,110 --> 00:03:52,736
And finally, there's a wooded area in the western section of the park, between

66
00:03:52,736 --> 00:03:53,600
two paths.

67
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:54,510
Okay,

68
00:03:54,510 --> 00:03:55,621
that's enough from me,

69
00:03:55,621 --> 00:03:57,400
so let's go on to…
